WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.213
How to proceed comes down to order.

2
00:00:02.213 --> 00:00:06.650
Order decides whether branch
modernization is a gain or a regression.

3
00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:08.962
Step zero: secure the governor.

4
00:00:08.962 --> 00:00:13.715
The SD-WAN controller and its edges are
internet-facing with estate-wide authority,

5
00:00:13.715 --> 00:00:16.332
so they come under
vulnerability management,

6
00:00:16.332 --> 00:00:20.051
privileged access and off-box
logging before they carry traffic.

7
00:00:20.051 --> 00:00:22.821
Step one: buy the pipe
on measured physics,

8
00:00:22.821 --> 00:00:26.325
latency and loss recorded
per site before the order.

9
00:00:26.325 --> 00:00:30.062
Step two: deploy the governor
before production traffic;

10
00:00:30.062 --> 00:00:34.913
a site whose control layer isn't live
and logging doesn't get its new egress.

11
00:00:34.913 --> 00:00:39.241
Step three: treat the boundary change
as the significant change it is,

12
00:00:39.241 --> 00:00:42.126
decided before the first
production cutover.

13
00:00:42.126 --> 00:00:48.388
Step four: handle Microsoft 365 Optimize
traffic through its own signed exception.

14
00:00:48.388 --> 00:00:50.661
Step five: register the evidence,

15
00:00:50.661 --> 00:00:55.375
and confirm CISA telemetry parity
before any legacy circuit ends.

16
00:00:55.375 --> 00:01:00.888
The book is candid that no memo, directive
or executive order sets this sequence.

17
00:01:00.888 --> 00:01:05.738
It's an engineering dependency, and saying
so is what makes it survive review.

18
00:01:05.738 --> 00:01:10.854
Doing it out of order, above all lighting
up fast circuits before the security layer

19
00:01:10.854 --> 00:01:15.600
is live, is in the program's experience
the most common and most costly mistake.

20
00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:21.054
The boundary package carries the evidence:
the path policy, failover test records,

21
00:01:21.054 --> 00:01:24.903
path telemetry, each exception
with its need and duration,

22
00:01:24.903 --> 00:01:28.512
CISA parity, and the known
limitations stated openly.

23
00:01:28.512 --> 00:01:32.475
And when funding becomes possible,
prove the case in your own estate.

24
00:01:32.475 --> 00:01:37.900
Instrument two comparable branches for
30 days, change one, measure 30 more.

25
00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:42.462
The difference in differences is an effect
size a budget examiner will accept.

26
00:01:42.462 --> 00:01:45.055
The decision: adopt this order as program

27
00:01:45.055 --> 00:01:47.930
policy before the first
production cutover.
